1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,444
Switch on a lamp with an open
shade, and stand it close to a wall.

2
00:00:04,844 --> 00:00:07,506
The light on the wall is not a circle.

3
00:00:07,506 --> 00:00:12,098
Its edges are two curves, one bending
up and one bending down, and they

4
00:00:12,098 --> 00:00:13,058
never close.

5
00:00:13,508 --> 00:00:15,943
Aarav saw this on his
bedroom wall last night.

6
00:00:16,293 --> 00:00:18,401
Two open curves from one lamp.

7
00:00:18,401 --> 00:00:19,530
What are they?

8
00:00:20,030 --> 00:00:24,958
The wall slices the cone of light, just
like the plane that cut both cones.

9
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:26,831
The curve is the hyperbola.

10
00:00:27,481 --> 00:00:31,804
Like the ellipse, a hyperbola has
two fixed points, called the foci.

11
00:00:32,204 --> 00:00:36,327
But this time, a hyperbola is the set
of all points where the difference

12
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:39,292
of the distances from the
two foci is a constant.

13
00:00:39,692 --> 00:00:40,764
Watch P move.

14
00:00:40,764 --> 00:00:44,815
Its distance to one focus is
in blue, to the other in gold.

15
00:00:45,215 --> 00:00:46,284
Eight and two.

16
00:00:46,284 --> 00:00:47,306
Ten and four.

17
00:00:47,306 --> 00:00:48,470
Eleven and five.

18
00:00:48,870 --> 00:00:52,879
The distances grow, but the bigger
one always beats the smaller one by

19
00:00:52,879 --> 00:00:53,779
six.

20
00:00:53,341 --> 00:00:56,328
On the other branch, it
is the other way round.

21
00:00:56,328 --> 00:00:57,228
Still six.

22
00:00:57,765 --> 00:00:58,665
Remember this.

23
00:00:58,652 --> 00:01:01,426
For an ellipse the distances
add up to a constant.

24
00:01:01,426 --> 00:01:03,894
For a hyperbola, they
differ by a constant.

25
00:01:04,594 --> 00:01:05,727
Now the parts.

26
00:01:05,727 --> 00:01:08,976
The line through the foci
is the transverse axis.

27
00:01:08,976 --> 00:01:11,664
The midpoint of the foci is the centre.

28
00:01:12,064 --> 00:01:16,488
The curve meets the transverse
axis at two vertices, two a apart.

29
00:01:16,488 --> 00:01:18,392
The foci are two c apart.

30
00:01:18,792 --> 00:01:20,215
Put P at a vertex.

31
00:01:20,215 --> 00:01:23,669
One distance is c plus a,
the other is c minus a.

32
00:01:23,669 --> 00:01:25,386
The difference is two a.

33
00:01:25,386 --> 00:01:27,663
So the fixed difference is two a.

34
00:01:28,413 --> 00:01:32,352
The foci sit outside the
vertices, so c is bigger than a.

35
00:01:32,352 --> 00:01:36,443
NCERT defines b by b squared
equals c squared minus a squared.

36
00:01:37,193 --> 00:01:41,376
So for a hyperbola, c squared
equals a squared plus b squared.

37
00:01:41,376 --> 00:01:46,222
The line through the centre, square to
the transverse axis, is the conjugate

38
00:01:46,222 --> 00:01:47,122
axis.

39
00:01:47,434 --> 00:01:48,741
Now the equation.

40
00:01:48,741 --> 00:01:51,959
Put the foci at minus c, zero and c, zero.

41
00:01:52,359 --> 00:01:53,259
Step one.

42
00:01:52,884 --> 00:01:54,829
The difference of the
two distances is two a.

43
00:01:55,579 --> 00:01:56,479
Step two.

44
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:58,754
Move one root across
and square both sides.

45
00:01:59,504 --> 00:02:00,404
Step three.

46
00:02:00,374 --> 00:02:02,463
Tidy up, and square once more.

47
00:02:03,213 --> 00:02:04,113
Step four.

48
00:02:04,056 --> 00:02:07,001
Swap c squared minus a
squared for b squared.

49
00:02:07,751 --> 00:02:08,815
Divide through.

50
00:02:08,815 --> 00:02:13,261
x squared over a squared, minus y
squared over b squared, equals one.

51
00:02:13,261 --> 00:02:16,044
Just one sign is different
from the ellipse.

52
00:02:16,694 --> 00:02:20,246
The eccentricity is c
over a, just as before.

53
00:02:20,646 --> 00:02:21,729
Watch e grow.

54
00:02:21,729 --> 00:02:25,241
The foci move out, and the
two branches open wider.

55
00:02:25,241 --> 00:02:28,924
Since c is bigger than a,
e is always more than one.

56
00:02:29,574 --> 00:02:30,621
Side by side.

57
00:02:30,621 --> 00:02:33,317
Ellipse: the distances add up to two a.

58
00:02:33,317 --> 00:02:37,525
c squared is a squared minus b
squared, and e is less than one.

59
00:02:37,925 --> 00:02:40,529
Hyperbola: the distances differ by two a.

60
00:02:40,529 --> 00:02:44,491
c squared is a squared plus b
squared, and e is more than one.

61
00:02:45,091 --> 00:02:45,996
Your turn.

62
00:02:45,996 --> 00:02:50,376
x squared over sixteen, minus y
squared over nine, equals one.

63
00:02:50,376 --> 00:02:51,874
Where are the foci?

64
00:02:51,874 --> 00:02:53,206
Pause and decide.

65
00:02:56,406 --> 00:02:58,650
At plus or minus five, zero!

66
00:02:58,650 --> 00:03:04,073
It is a hyperbola, so c squared is
sixteen plus nine, which is twenty five.

67
00:03:04,723 --> 00:03:06,413
Now, one worked example.

68
00:03:06,763 --> 00:03:11,307
For nine y squared minus sixteen x
squared equals one hundred forty four,

69
00:03:11,307 --> 00:03:14,819
find the foci, the eccentricity
and the latus rectum.

70
00:03:15,319 --> 00:03:16,219
Step one.

71
00:03:16,192 --> 00:03:18,599
Divide by one hundred forty four.

72
00:03:18,599 --> 00:03:23,082
y squared over sixteen, minus x
squared over nine, equals one.

73
00:03:23,832 --> 00:03:24,732
Step two.

74
00:03:24,663 --> 00:03:28,696
The plus term is y, so the
transverse axis is the y axis.

75
00:03:28,696 --> 00:03:30,530
a is four, b is three.

76
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:32,196
Step three.

77
00:03:32,196 --> 00:03:35,379
c squared is sixteen
plus nine, so c is five.

78
00:03:35,379 --> 00:03:38,095
The foci are zero, plus or minus five.

79
00:03:38,845 --> 00:03:39,745
Step four.

80
00:03:39,665 --> 00:03:41,888
The eccentricity is five over four.

81
00:03:41,888 --> 00:03:46,071
The latus rectum is two b squared
over a, which is nine over two.

82
00:03:46,721 --> 00:03:48,185
Now, the exam trap.

83
00:03:48,535 --> 00:03:52,548
x squared over nine, minus y
squared over sixteen, equals one.

84
00:03:52,548 --> 00:03:57,057
Many students say a squared is sixteen,
because it is the bigger number.

85
00:03:57,457 --> 00:03:59,803
But that rule is only for the ellipse.

86
00:03:59,803 --> 00:04:02,926
In a hyperbola, a squared
sits under the plus term.

87
00:04:02,926 --> 00:04:04,960
So a is three, and c is five.

88
00:04:05,610 --> 00:04:07,082
Where is this asked?

89
00:04:07,082 --> 00:04:08,100
In JEE Main.

90
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:12,467
In January twenty twenty four, a
question asked for the eccentricity of

91
00:04:12,467 --> 00:04:14,898
a hyperbola, built from an ellipse.

92
00:04:15,498 --> 00:04:16,764
Exam level now.

93
00:04:16,764 --> 00:04:21,848
A hyperbola, x squared over a squared
minus y squared over b squared equals

94
00:04:21,848 --> 00:04:26,642
one, has eccentricity five over
three, and its foci are ten apart.

95
00:04:26,642 --> 00:04:28,348
Find its latus rectum.

96
00:04:28,348 --> 00:04:29,667
Pause and solve.

97
00:04:35,067 --> 00:04:36,496
The answer is B.

98
00:04:36,496 --> 00:04:38,258
Thirty two over three.

99
00:04:38,758 --> 00:04:41,979
The foci are ten apart, so c is five.

100
00:04:41,979 --> 00:04:44,729
e is c over a, so a is three.

101
00:04:45,229 --> 00:04:47,850
b squared is c squared minus a squared.

102
00:04:47,850 --> 00:04:50,109
Twenty five minus nine is sixteen.

103
00:04:50,609 --> 00:04:53,224
The latus rectum is two b squared over a.

104
00:04:53,224 --> 00:04:56,493
Two times sixteen over three
is thirty two over three.

105
00:04:57,093 --> 00:04:58,633
Here is your recap.

106
00:04:58,633 --> 00:05:00,216
Screenshot this card.

107
00:05:03,416 --> 00:05:05,602
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

108
00:05:06,002 --> 00:05:06,902
One.

109
00:05:06,436 --> 00:05:09,328
What stays the same for
every point on a hyperbola?

110
00:05:10,228 --> 00:05:11,128
Two.

111
00:05:10,751 --> 00:05:15,860
For x squared over nine, minus y
squared over seven, equals one, find c.

112
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:17,660
Three.

113
00:05:17,343 --> 00:05:21,082
Why is the eccentricity of a
hyperbola always more than one?

114
00:05:22,182 --> 00:05:25,162
Next time: where exactly
is the fan in your room?

115
00:05:25,162 --> 00:05:26,827
Two numbers are not enough.

116
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:28,624
We step into three dimensions.
